      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Remote-mount a harness",
      "prov:value": "The owner, 2026-10-06, ruled on how a downstream folio gets the layers it is\nbuilt on:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two halves of the declaration",
      "prov:value": "Code the mounted graphs import has to\nsit in a declared directory (owner, 2026-10-07: \"Forks declare it\", bean\n`hupw`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two halves of the declaration",
      "prov:value": "**Every tool that writes mounts writes through `writeDeclaredMounts`**, into\n`index.config.json`, and none writes `remoteMounts` any more."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two halves of the declaration",
      "prov:value": "An id may be one the instance\n  declares in its `<name>.json` **or from within** one of those directories\n  (a `\"subgraph\": true` entry of `skills/skills.json`, such as `voices`);\n  both are resolved at the pin through `instanceDirectories`, the resolver\n  every on-disk reader uses (bean `mo75` G3, after `2j2r`). A nested id mounts\n  its own path alone.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mo75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The two halves of the declaration",
      "prov:value": "- `hydrated: true` (here, or on the entry for its harness) mounts each chosen\n  directory as one file: its published `index.hydrated.jsonld` at the pin, a\n  `hydrated` source (bean `mo75`). Read what is there, then choose what to\n  mount as files.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mo75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Hydrated: the index files are published per pin, in a package",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-24 (decision card, option A): **a pin's subgraph index files\n(`index.jsonld`, `index.hydrated.jsonld` under `<docs>/subgraph/<HARNESS>/`)\nare published per pin in a package**, and a hydrated mount fetches them\nthrough the Tool its source names (the `hydrated` source's `tool`, which is\n`remote-mount` unless it says otherwise; bean `j9cs`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean j9cs",
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Hydrated: the index files are published per pin, in a package",
      "prov:value": "The files are `builtAtPublish`:\n  they are computed over the checkout's other instances, so no commit can\n  hold them current, and a committed copy turns every re-pin's check red\n  (owner, 2026-10-14, \"B1\").",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tools: choose by id, mount runnable",
      "prov:value": "The owner's workflow (bean `mo75`): load the Tools' metadata, review it,\nthen materialise a chosen set.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mo75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tools: choose by id, mount runnable",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-24 (decision card on\n[cat-harness-tools#744](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/744), all four as\nrecommended).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#744",
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tools: choose by id, mount runnable",
      "prov:value": "**What it costs, measured** on cat-harness main (2026-10-24). A Tool folder is\nnot a declared directory: `tools/` is, and most definitions import its\n`lib.ts`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The lock, and the three states",
      "prov:value": "It is generated by `mount:remote` and never hand-edited, which\nis why it is a separate file rather than part of the index. Until 2026-10-07 it\nwas `<name>.mount-lock.json`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The lock, and the three states",
      "prov:value": "A path that block does not cover is\nreported as missing, never patched locally, because a local exclude is\ninvisible to every other clone. A folio with no index keeps the old behaviour:\na path its rules do not ignore goes into the worktree's `info/exclude`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The lock, and the three states",
      "prov:value": "**Mount path and route collisions (bean folio-assistant-t4xb).** A mount with no `path`\noverride lands at `<name>/` in the downstream root, beside the downstream's own\ndirectories, and its site routes sit beside the site-wide ones.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-t4xb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Re-pinning: from a checkout mounted from the lock",
      "prov:value": "A\nmount with local edits is left untouched by the next mount, at its old\ncommit, while the lock's top-level pin moves; CI mounts from the instance\nentries, so it kept testing the old layer (folio-assistant#2682). `--seed`\nnow refuses while a mount it moves has such edits, and `mount:check` reports\nan instance entry behind its pin as `missing`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2682"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "A changed lock re-renders the agent surface",
      "prov:value": "That is what happened on folio-assistant#2526, whose re-pin shipped the new\nlayers with the old memory and went red on three agent-memory tests.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2526"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Trust: what lets a mount proceed (H8)",
      "prov:value": "Four\nthings to know (roast `1ygp` L4.2):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "`1ygp`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Standing consent: a site keeps itself on an upstream branch",
      "prov:value": "Pins stay per site (owner, 2026-10-16). A site may\ndeclare, on one instance's `trust.standing`, that a named person consents\nto following a branch — `{follows: \"main\", consentBy, consentAt, require?:\n\"green\"}`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Publishing a remote-mounted downstream — provision `gh-pages` first",
      "prov:value": "A downstream that publishes a site needs a `gh-pages`\nbranch before GitHub Pages can be switched on, exactly as a new repository\ndoes. Owner, 2026-10-01: *\"need to create gh-pages branch before can turn\non\"*; repeated 2026-10-07: *\"need to create gh-pages before can deploy\"*\n(issue #2417).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2417",
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/remote-mount.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Publishing a remote-mounted downstream — provision `gh-pages` first",
      "prov:value": "The worked example is litlfred/test — an overlay with remote mounts, its\n`gh-pages` provisioned as `860f9c2` in litlfred/test#5 — written up in\n[`repo-conversion`](../../conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md) §5."
    },
    {
